{#- diagnostic_prompt.j2 — GraphRAG prompt for incident playbooks (REQ-H).
    Variables: component (dict), dependencies (list), anomalies (list),
    unhealthy (list), now (str), max_steps (int). -#}
An incident is predicted on the component `{{ component.node_id }}` of an event-processing platform
(Kafka ingestion, Prometheus, ML forecasting and diagnostics services, running in Kubernetes
namespace `event-processor` or docker compose). Diagnose the most likely root cause and write a
remediation playbook for an on-call engineer.

Current time (UTC): {{ now }}

## Component under investigation
- id: {{ component.node_id }}
- type: {{ component.node_type }}
- health: {{ component.health_status }}
- version: {{ component.metadata.version }}
- owner team: {{ component.metadata.owner_team }}
- SLA tier: {{ component.metadata.sla_tier }}
- last deployed at: {{ component.metadata.last_deployed_at }}

## Predicted anomalies (from the forecasting service, p90 forecast)
{% if anomalies -%}
{% for a in anomalies -%}
- {{ a | tojson }}
{% endfor -%}
{% else -%}
- none supplied (on-demand diagnosis)
{% endif %}
## Dependency subgraph (2 hops; downstream = this component depends on it, upstream = depends on this component)
{% if dependencies -%}
| node | type | health | edge | direction | depth | via | owner | last deployed |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for d in dependencies -%}
| {{ d.node_id }} | {{ d.node_type }} | {{ d.health_status }} | {{ d.edge_type }} | {{ d.direction }} | {{ d.depth }} | {{ d.via }} | {{ d.metadata.owner_team }} | {{ d.metadata.last_deployed_at }} |
{% endfor -%}
{% else -%}
(no dependencies recorded)
{% endif %}
{% if unhealthy -%}
Unhealthy dependencies: {{ unhealthy | join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
## Instructions
1. Use only the facts above; if evidence is weak, say so in the hypothesis.
2. Prefer causes in downstream dependencies that are degraded/down, then resource pressure on the
   component itself, then recent deployments.
3. Produce between 3 and {{ max_steps }} steps ranked by priority (rank 1 = do first): diagnostic
   checks first, then mitigations, then follow-ups. Commands must be safe, read-only where possible,
   and concrete (kubectl / curl / kafka CLI). Destructive actions must say so in the title.

## Output format
Respond with a single JSON object and nothing else (no prose, no Markdown fences), exactly:
{
  "summary": "<one sentence describing the incident>",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "<most likely root cause and the evidence for it>",
  "steps": [
    {"rank": 1, "title": "<short imperative action>", "command": "<shell command or empty string>", "expected_outcome": "<what success looks like>"}
  ]
}
